    "created_at": "2016-07-18T17:18:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-18T17:18:32Z",
    "body": "Seems to have gotten lost a bit thanks to the W3C messing with bugs: https://www.w3.org/Bugs/Public/show_bug.cgi?id=16970#c15.\n\nBut in general we have quite a few concepts that lowercase ASCII code points and then compare case-sensitive. However, when observed casually that appears as an ASCII case-insensitive comparison. E.g., HTML parser, CSS parser, Selectors, DOM.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
