    "created_at": "2016-07-18T18:10:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-07-18T18:10:19Z",
    "body": "@annevk is correct - excepting obvious actual Unicode-handling APIs, the platform _intentionally_ doesn't care about normalization.  A given string's context is either ASCII, in which case we can do CI comparisons, or all of Unicode, in which case we do codepoint-comparisons.  CSS definitely follows this very intentionally.\n\nIf you have multiple authors providing different normalizations in your codebase, uh, fix that.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
